{
	"name": "Leshling",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/magic/nature/stealth-hide-eyes-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Those who spend any length of time in the untamed wilds have undoubtedly encountered a leshling before. Tiny spirits of the forest, leshlings are made of the plant material that dominates the biome that they call home and frequently carry a lantern that is full of fireflies or another similar light source. Their most prominent feature are a pair of glowing orange eyes that are embedded in the inky darkness that comprises their interiors.</p><p>So long as adventurers do not bring harm to the wilderness that a leshling is found in, they will act as benign guides, providing information regarding important landmarks or other areas of interest. If they are harmed or otherwise angered by the party’s actions, however, leshlings will send out a distress call, summoning @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-monsters.Actor.Fuzzxz5Ng6eKA7RD]{Aluraru, Warden of the Forest}, who appears within 30 feet of the party in [[/r 1d4]] hours.</p>",
